From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/47] PC5: a loopback network interface for games that list
 them (Wine patch 0934)

A title starts no other process, so Wine's network information service
(nsiproxy.sys) never ran, and every call that lists the network
interfaces or their addresses failed with error 2. Java's
NetworkInterface throws an Error on that, and SecureRandom's seeding
uses it: Shattered Pixel Dungeon closed when it started a new game.
Wine's nsi.dll answers those calls itself now, with the loopback
interface Windows always has (127.0.0.1 and ::1).
---
